        ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
        ":question/problem": "What is the value of ${\\int }_{8}^{64}\\frac{1}{x\\sqrt{{log}_{8}\u2061x}}\\,\\text{d}x?$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "Let $u={log}_{8}\u2061x.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}\u20618}\\,\u27f9\\,\\operatorname{ln}\u20618\\,\\text{d}u=\\frac{\\text{d}x}{x}.\n$$\n\nCalculating the limits for $u$ gives the following:\n\n| $x$ | $8$ | $64$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $1$ | $2$ |\n\nWe now substitute and evaluate as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{8}^{64}\\frac{1}{x\\sqrt{{log}_{8}\u2061x}}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{8}^{64}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{log}_{8}\u2061x}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{x} \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{u}}\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}\u20618\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}\u20618{\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{u}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}\u20618(2\\sqrt{u}){|}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{ln}\u20618(\\sqrt{2}-\\sqrt{1}) \\\\  & =2(\\sqrt{2}-1)\\operatorname{ln}\u20618\\end{aligned}\n$$",
